        5,
        9,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.greensburgks.org/1257/About-Greensburg-History",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town is home to the world’s largest hand‑dug well, the Big Well, which began construction in 1887 and was completed in 1888.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        26,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greensburg%2C_Kansas",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Big Well was declared a national museum in 1972.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greensburg%2C_Kansas",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Greensburg’s new hospital, city hall, and school were built to LEED certification standards, the highest level issued by the organization.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greensburg%2C_Kansas",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "A meteorite weighing over 1,000 pounds, one of the largest pallasites, was discovered near Greensburg in 1949.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
